Z||000005||fldevel||05-03-2001||07:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B> It wont affect it at all. Your still using the stock Alt. pulley. The new crank pulley is smaller & will rotate faster, thus charging the battery quicker.    <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>um if the drive pully is smaller wont it rotate slower ? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wolfhound||05-03-2001||07:19 PM||||Actually the alternator will rotate slower, as well as the water pump and AC compressor. It shouldn,t effect out put much at all.<BR>The purpose is to slow driven accessories and and reduce the work load the engines crank. <BR>Coy||||reg||1
